<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mylae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mylae was an ancient Greek city on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, founded by settlers from Zancle in the 8th century BCE on the site of modern Milazzo. Off its coast in 260 BCE the Roman fleet, using the boarding bridge known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corvus">corvus</a>, won its first great naval victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. The town later belonged to Messana and to Roman Sicily.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mylae.jpg" alt="Mylae" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clemensfranz · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Milazzo_Stadtansicht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
